{
  "slug": "search-insert-position",
  "title": "Search Insert Position",
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": [
    "array",
    "binary-search"
  ],
  "license": "MIT",
  "source": {
    "name": "Mockify seed set"
  },
  "description": "Given a sorted array of distinct integers and a `target`, return the index of `target` if it exists, otherwise the index where it **would be inserted** to keep the array sorted. Aim for O(log n).\n\n### Input\n- Line 1: `nums`, space-separated integers.\n- Line 2: `target`, an integer.\n\n### Output\nOne integer.\n\n### Constraints\n- `1 <= nums.length <= 6000`\n- `-10^4 <= nums[i] <= 10^4`\n- `nums` is sorted ascending with no duplicates.",
  "signature": {
    "params": [
      {
        "name": "nums",
        "type": "int[]"
      },
      {
        "name": "target",
        "type": "int"
      }
    ],
    "returns": "int"
  },
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": "1 3 5 6\n5\n",
      "output": "2\n"
    },
    {
      "input": "1 3 5 6\n2\n",
      "output": "1\n",
      "explanation": "2 goes between 1 and 3."
    },
    {
      "input": "1 3 5 6\n7\n",
      "output": "4\n"
    }
  ],
